 "result_text": "Equation fields now keep Knack's own formatted value in `.formatted`, so your `field_377` examples should give 4 and 5 (days) rather than the raw seconds. `.raw` is unchanged. I haven't run it against real Knack data. I only checked that `knackpy` still imports.\n\nThe fix is in two places:\n- **`models.py`:** I added `\"equation\": {\"use_knack_format\": True}` to `FIELD_SETTINGS`. This is the same setting that timer, name and id fields already use.\n- **`fields.py`:** `Field._format` used to fall back to the raw value whenever the Knack-formatted value was falsy. That would have made an equation result of `0` come out as the raw value, so it now falls back only when the Knack-formatted value is `None`.\n\nNo tests were added or changed, and nothing is committed.",
